    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. So I've joined with right now, I think we're up to two dozen members of the house. quite frankly we should have a hundred fifty members of the house calling for this about and uh... and what we've said is and we laid out very carefully in a uh... many pages uh... very detailed way uh... on three areas that the department of justice and the fb i had trouble uh... they've been perhaps even corrupt okay let's just let's put it that way It was, and it was for political purposes. So we started with the Hillary Clinton investigation. They exonerate her. There's so many problems with how they did that investigation and the determination to exonerate from everything from writing the exoneration letter before you finish interviewing more than a dozen witnesses to the meeting of Lynch and former President Clinton on the term act in Phoenix. So that's one area. The second area is the FISA warrants and the misleading documents, the dossier that's fraudulent and everyone knows it's fraudulent. The failure to disclose information when getting the FISA warrants so that they could spy on American citizens. And then the third area that we're talking about is just the the manipulation and creation of this Russian investigation, which is now so far afield, that two things that the listeners need to be really aware of is that the special counsel is Robert Mueller. His staff now are filing documents into court to get themselves classified as Department of Justice employees as special prosecutors. That's what they want to do. So you see, they moved and they want authority now to be able to prosecute as opposed to being special counsel. This is so far a field. It's not funny. And so that's what we're doing. And we're demanding that attorney general Jeff Sessions stand up, retake the wing, the handles of this investigation and give us a new counsel, special counsel. Why? Because the DOJ and FBI are implicated at the highest level. It's not the rank and file, but at the highest levels of political corruption. And they can't investigate themselves. So we need a separate independent investigator.",
