  {
    "episode_id": 87320,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/7/87320.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "Is it go to this larger issue, Andy? I mean, yeah, we'll take a minute on this. Does it go to this larger issue? I've long talked about, which is that somehow there's a media entertainment culture. There's a sophisticated culture. I use the word sophisticated in quotes, but you know what I'm talking about. That just simply has a different standard for Republicans and Democrats because Republicans to them are something to be kind of tolerated once in a while, but certainly not a real party, not a real movement, not anything that has the right to govern. So, you know, if things are being done to them wrongly, if things are being done to them even illegally, you know, who really cares? It's not really a story because they're not really legitimate in the first place. They don't think we're legitimate. That's what it comes down to.",
