    "turn_text": "what what you know i think it's more fundamental than that it is almost a de-humanization of those who disagree with them i mean the way you when you need to think of this is they they've used themselves at the tolerant class and yet their took so totally intolerant of anyone who is a dissenting opinion that's why you get these crazy things like a free speech zone on university campuses where you have to go to an isolated area to say what your true political beliefs are. It is dehumanization, and that is very, very dangerous, particularly in constitutional republic, but within any society to dehumanize anyone. That's problematic.",
