    "turn_idx": 69,
    "turn_text": "It's going to be an odd thing, I think, if too many people get too far ahead of their skis on this NFL policy. How many times do the American people and the protesters who want to take a knee during the National Anthem need to be taught that this is something up with which the American people really don't want to put? It's just not something that they're very interested in, downgrading American patriotism. This is a problem the Left has had for a long time to begin with. I don't know why they'd want to double down on it. If this is something more and more democratic party officials want to weigh in on, then we'll add it to the list of things they think they're going to create a blue wave with. That list now comprises basically raising your taxes and undoing the juggernaut of the American economy that we have seen unleashed over the past year or so. It would include not asking people their citizenship status on the census. It would include putting the IRS back into your healthcare decision-making processes. And it would include increasing regulations to the point of lowering employment in the small business community. Add that, add that, add all that, add that menu to arguing that, to arguing that it is jingoistic to have the players in the NFL stand for the national anthem. And I think you're gonna, you're gonna find yourself a party without a business.",
